metag: the module offset of a general-dynamic local symbol

For general-dynamic access to a symbol that binds locally -- a static
__thread variable, which gcc reaches through general-dynamic at -O0 --
relocate_section wrote the DTPMOD relocation and left the second GOT word,
the offset in the module's TLS block, at 0.  Every such variable then
resolved to the start of the block: uClibc-ng's tst-tls10 and tst-tls11,
whose modules are built without optimisation, read local1 from there.

The offset is known at link time, as for the initial-exec entry below:
relocation - dtpoff_base.

diff --git a/bfd/elf32-metag.c b/bfd/elf32-metag.c
index 7a56eea..293abf1 100644
--- a/bfd/elf32-metag.c
+++ b/bfd/elf32-metag.c
@@ -1797,8 +1797,11 @@ elf_metag_relocate_section (struct bfd_link_info *info,
 			htab->etab.srelgot->reloc_count++;
 			loc += sizeof (Elf32_External_Rela);
 
+			/* A symbol that binds locally has its offset in the
+			   module's block known now.  */
 			if (indx == 0)
-			  bfd_put_32 (info->output_bfd, 0,
+			  bfd_put_32 (info->output_bfd,
+				      relocation - dtpoff_base (info),
 				      htab->etab.sgot->contents + cur_off + 4);
 			else
 			  {
